<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18189" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fimbrĭa</span></b> , ae, m.
		fimbriae. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Roman surname in the</i> gens Flavia.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> C. Flavius Fimbria,
				<i>consul</i> A. U. C. 650; <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 70, § 181</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id.
				Planc. 21, 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 2, 22,
			91</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Another of the same name, <i>an enemy of M.
			Crassus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 66, 233</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rosc.
				Am. 12, 33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fimbrĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj.: seditio, Sall. Fragm. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 215, 32</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
